        "original_id": "53830799-7758-5d40-8701-e24bdb6a8ed0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Zane Grey, Bhabananda Deka\n- Roles: dentist, author, economist\n- Topics: Western genre, American frontier, economy of northeastern India\n\nFacts:\n- Pearl Zane Grey was born on January 31, 1872, and died on October 23, 1939.\n- Pearl Zane Grey was an American dentist and author known for popular adventure novels and stories associated with the Western genre.\n- Zane Grey idealized the American frontier.\n- Bhabananda Deka was born on August 19, 1929, and died on December 4, 2006.\n- Bhabananda Deka was an Assamese economist and author.\n- Bhabananda Deka has been acknowledged as a pioneering Assam economist who conducted path-breaking early research on the economy of the far eastern part of India.",
